&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=moon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;moon&quot;&gt;moon&lt;/a&gt;, I think this line is the cluprit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/sravan-s/zeppelin/blob/master/zeppelin-web/src/app/visualization/builtins/visualization-piechart.js#L51&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/sravan-s/zeppelin/blob/master/zeppelin-web/src/app/visualization/builtins/visualization-piechart.js#L51&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regardless of if grouping happened or not, only d&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; is taken for drawing the chart.&lt;br/&gt;
But when data is grouped, it comes in all the elements of the array&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15903920" author="moon" created="Thu, 9 Mar 2017 21:53:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for taking care of this issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think all groups can be merged and displayed in a single pie chart,&lt;br/&gt;
Or each group can have it&apos;s own pie chart, so multiple pie charts are displayed when group exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15904387" author="ess_ess" created="Fri, 10 Mar 2017 03:56:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes, I was also thinking about displaying all charts in a single pie chart. I personally like something like this: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.amcharts.com/demos/pie-chart-broken-slices/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://www.amcharts.com/demos/pie-chart-broken-slices/&lt;/a&gt; , with each group as a broken slice inside the main sector, not sure if it is possible within the boundaries of NVD3. I made a starter branch at github, which I will modify as things get more clearer &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think each group can having it&apos;s own pie chart would end up a bit heavy for the UI&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
